    "text": "Elin Gow is an Irish smith and hero. He tended the wonderful cow, a beast that gave her milk in endless plenty, so that none who kept her ever went short of food. The cow was hard to hold, but Elin kept step with her for seven full years, which no man had done before. He brought the cow to Ireland and gave her into the care of a man named Cian. When Cian fell asleep, Balor, a king of the Fomorians, came and stole the cow away.",
